That balance is exactly the \textbf{energy balance in a series loop}: charge that goes once around
must finish with the same energy it started with, so
\[
\mathcal{E}=V_1+V_2+\cdots
\]
For a total charge $Q$ around the loop, the cell supplies $\mathcal{E}Q$ and the loads convert
$V_1Q+V_2Q+\cdots$; each transfer follows $E=VQ$ (or $E=\mathcal{E}Q$ in the source).

