\noindent\textbf{Question-bank method.}
Every mixed circuit in the QB can be solved by \emph{colouring the wires} and tracking
potential --- no $R_{\mathrm{eq}}$ and no $I=\mathcal{E}/R_{\mathrm{eq}}$ is needed.
Same colour $\Rightarrow$ equipotential ($V=0$ between those points).
Different colours with a component between them $\Rightarrow$ p.d.\ $=E/Q$ (energy per coulomb),
or $V=IR$ on \emph{one} resistor in a branch at a time.

\begin{center}
\begin{circuitikz}[scale=1.05, transform shape]
  \draw (0,0.9) to[battery1, l_=$6\,\mathrm{V}$] (0,2.5);
