\ex
An electron moves through a network of identical resistors from terminal $P$ to $O$ to $N$ to $M$.
Where is its energy change the \emph{greatest}?
\sol[2.5cm]{%
Compare $|\Delta V|$ between consecutive points along the path ($E=e\Delta V$).
The largest p.d.\ step --- found by colouring wires and reading potential drops --- gives the
greatest energy change; no resistance values are needed.
}

