Three resistors are connected to a battery as shown. The circuit is earthed at point~$G$.
When one coulomb of charge flows along path $ACDEB$, it loses $2\,\mathrm{J}$ in $CD$ and
$5\,\mathrm{J}$ in $DE$.
Find the e.m.f.\ $\mathcal{E}$ of the battery, and hence the potential at each point
(let the earthed point be zero).
\begin{center}
\begin{circuitikz}[scale=1.05, transform shape]
  \draw (0,3.0) node[circ]{} node[font=\scriptsize,left] at (-0.12,3.0) {$A$}
        -- (0,1.5) node[circ]{} node[font=\scriptsize,left] at (-0.12,1.5) {$C$}
        -- (0,0) node[circ]{} node[font=\scriptsize,left] at (-0.12,0) {$F$};
  \draw (5.0,3.0) node[circ]{} node[font=\scriptsize,right] at (5.12,3.0) {$B$}
        -- (5.0,1.5) node[circ]{} node[font=\scriptsize,right] at (5.12,1.5) {$E$}
        -- (5.0,0) node[circ]{} node[font=\scriptsize,right] at (5.12,0) {$G$};
  \draw (0,3.0) to[battery1, l=$\mathcal{E}$] (5.0,3.0);
  \draw (0,1.5) to[R] (2.5,1.5) node[circ]{} node[font=\scriptsize,below] at (2.5,1.35) {$D$}
        to[R] (5.0,1.5);
  \draw (0,0) to[R] (5.0,0);
  \draw (5.0,0) -- (5.8,0);
  \node[ground] at (5.8,0) {};
\end{circuitikz}
\end{center}
\sol[5.0cm]{%
$V_G=0$. Points $B$, $E$ and $G$ share an ideal wire $\Rightarrow$ $V_B=V_E=0$.
Points $A$, $C$ and $F$ share the left wire $\Rightarrow$ equipotential.
Along $ACDEB$: drop in $CD$ is $2\,\mathrm{V}$, in $DE$ is $5\,\mathrm{V}$, so
$V_A-V_B=2+5=7\,\mathrm{V}$ $\Rightarrow$ $\mathcal{E}=7\,\mathrm{V}$ and $V_A=V_C=V_F=7\,\mathrm{V}$.
Then $V_D=V_C-2=5\,\mathrm{V}$.
\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{@{}ccccccc@{}}
\toprule
Point & $A$ & $B$ & $C$ & $D$ & $E$ & $F$ & $G$ \\
\midrule
Potential & $7\,\mathrm{V}$ & $0$ & $7\,\mathrm{V}$ & $5\,\mathrm{V}$ & $0$ & $7\,\mathrm{V}$ & $0$ \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{center}
}

