So far, $R$ describes a whole component. For a uniform conductor,
\[
R=\rho\,\frac{\ell}{A},
\]
where $\rho$ is the \textbf{resistivity} of the material (unit $\Omega\,\mathrm{m}$).
Same material: longer ($\ell\uparrow$) $\Rightarrow$ larger $R$; thicker wire ($A\uparrow$)
